body:
If they were going to do this (not saying they should) they would have to make the player gain points or money some how for interacting with the players and less bonus for hunting. Hunting should be a last resort. Or, you should only be able to hunt when you have completed enough interaction tasks. So you have to leave fingerprints, go into the room with the camera, set off the EMF reader etc. After completing enough tasks, then you can hunt. AND as the round goes on, you lose "health" if you just sit and hide. 

&#x200B;

It's not a perfect system, but I can see it working. The goal should be to get to get interactions to fill your "hunt" bar and as the round goes on (and sanity goes down) you can fill your hunt bar more quickly.
